     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is high.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 1,700 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, split some other way.\n- **Something else.**\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm it. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
