     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm sorry, but I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled dose. Nothing in the patient's profile, such as normal kidney and liver function, justifies that. The risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is too high for me to put it in the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose.\n- **Enter a lower dose.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily, or a dose titrated up from a lower starting point.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or the attending.** If you think this dose is clinically necessary, they can review it and enter it through their own process. I can draft a note for that review.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
